{"event_type":"review","id":"19d9aff3a45f68a4ca05a999ce5802638233c70a8f30b1fb9f45538071d86ac2","occurred_at":"2026-11-15T00:49:35Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/ee13ada5230b73c77ca028919468bc31155cef8294f6ab8a3c84823fddee0afe","sha256":"ee13ada5230b73c77ca028919468bc31155cef8294f6ab8a3c84823fddee0afe"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/3a27497a466299c78762dbb791580568ddb7f4a9a99fff1d8a5f556bd1e51308","sha256":"3a27497a466299c78762dbb791580568ddb7f4a9a99fff1d8a5f556bd1e51308"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/0dd9dd51fb45920f1363144e52a34ee18f5ec5853c8b1a346ece1c32fb57f859","sha256":"0dd9dd51fb45920f1363144e52a34ee18f5ec5853c8b1a346ece1c32fb57f859"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/5d225962ea40cdbea1b5ad1334fab02d2a8b23d7107536b8ff3cf41e4317b2eb","sha256":"5d225962ea40cdbea1b5ad1334fab02d2a8b23d7107536b8ff3cf41e4317b2eb"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/6b2d1460a433172f4d9c1c25511e2aecc0668c7a60c7af3e2d1d4136b4e76362","sha256":"6b2d1460a433172f4d9c1c25511e2aecc0668c7a60c7af3e2d1d4136b4e76362"}],"attempt_id":"b55f95c3ebae2ca258903f586c0288bdcd40a9418eeb219bfbd5a1e1ecb0e11d:0:1","base":"b33cac4bd9fda973b6ac46d3e6e25f8fca6f8d62","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"39b4711272945983ce677369a7e96f50d825cf59","body":"**Scan legacy source snapshots before any driver receives them.**\n\nFor a drained job without `revalidation`, `source_snapshot` skips the prepared-source binding and returns an excerpt of the pinned source. The excerpt covers up to 40 lines before and 40 lines after `finding.line`, capped at 16,000 characters (`apps/crq-python/crq_repair/bounded.py:228-244`). The dispatch path stores this excerpt on the job at `apps/crq-python/crq_repair.py:331` before the selected driver runs. No secret scan runs on that path. Prepared jobs get a full-blob scan in `prepare_current_job` (`apps/crq-python/repair_tick.py:91-101`), and that code states that the denylist and gitleaks policy \"precedes any model use\". Legacy jobs skip that step. The Paseo judge serializes the whole job into its prompt (`apps/crq-python/crq_repair/drivers/paseo.py:27-30`), so a policy-detectable secret within the excerpt can reach the Paseo host.\n\nRun the same full-blob scan against `source_sha` for jobs without `revalidation`, as `repair_tick.py:99` does. Fail closed when the scan does not pass, and make that scan run before the snapshot is built. A scan of the review diff does not cover secrets elsewhere in the excerpt.","id":"174ba4dfc743751e6f6f61e55f51269f0b54e5dce504115a8e7ef2e1e79b2a8f","intervals":[[331,331]],"path":"apps/crq-python/crq_repair.py","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Scan legacy source snapshots before any driver receives them."},{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"39b4711272945983ce677369a7e96f50d825cf59","body":"**Write one JSON result for every `main` exit path.**\n\nAt `apps/crq-python/crq_repair.py:1278-1280`, a valid `--job` run calls `process_item(config, [job])` and returns. `process_item` returns only a status string or `None`. Neither it nor `process` calls `write_result`, so the run writes nothing to stdout. The drain branch, the disabled and blackout exits, and the deferred exits also return without a JSON artifact. Only the recovery branch and the triage dry-run call `write_result`.\n\nDoctrine I1 requires every operation invocation to write one machine-readable JSON artifact to stdout. This CLI already follows that contract on two paths, so I1 applies to all of its exits.\n\nMake `process_item` return the terminal result for its job. Have `main` pass that result to `write_result`. Preserve the `RUNNER_DISABLED_OUTCOME`, `'rate-limit'`, and `None` values that `drain_item` consumes, or update that caller in the same change. Emit exactly one artifact on each `main` exit, including the `runner_disabled` exit.","id":"f0e2779a6dc5aaacf722487572b1691ec32fbd9e5af4dca67b4f3b3761959d28","intervals":[[1279,1280]],"path":"apps/crq-python/crq_repair.py","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Write one JSON result for every `main` exit path."}],"head":"b6c56a8551d11e3a3bfd3b2edefc07ba16ad81a6","head_tree":"bda143e5c3801b7c35ed31c000807c5f716cf6f6","input_scope":[{"blob":"39b4711272945983ce677369a7e96f50d825cf59","intervals":[[1,1285]],"path":"apps/crq-python/crq_repair.py"},{"blob":"4fac438e88d0b3ed21c3ef5ed91f6e8274b59e86","intervals":[[1,616]],"path":"apps/crq-python/notify_coverage_vector_emit_b1.py"},{"blob":"34556dc326cd06165a9ec93ba758f6525954bfc2","intervals":[[1,994]],"path":"apps/crq-python/test_deploy_controller_unit_switch.py"},{"blob":"e266dfb6ccbb898b49b190c4e8128dedb95fe411","intervals":[[1,812]],"path":"apps/crq-python/test_repair_bounded.py"}],"job_id":"b55f95c3ebae2ca258903f586c0288bdcd40a9418eeb219bfbd5a1e1ecb0e11d:0","outcome":"completed","paths":[{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"39b4711272945983ce677369a7e96f50d825cf59","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"apps/crq-python/crq_repair.py","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"4fac438e88d0b3ed21c3ef5ed91f6e8274b59e86","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"apps/crq-python/notify_coverage_vector_emit_b1.py","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"34556dc326cd06165a9ec93ba758f6525954bfc2","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"apps/crq-python/test_deploy_controller_unit_switch.py","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"e266dfb6ccbb898b49b190c4e8128dedb95fe411","disposition":"included","